  "solution": {
    "brief": "Surface created from curves",
    "principle": "\n\nRelated insight: Recipe complexity scaling: Surface creation workflows can range from simple parametric sequences to complex 28+ component recipes like '11-3'.\n\nRelated insight: Specific complexity example: S11E04 demonstrates 59-component surface creation recipes, showing the upper range of parametric workflow complexity.\n\nRelated insight: Additional complexity example: Recipe '12-5' demonstrates 40-component surface creation workflows, fitting between simpler parametric sequences and the most complex 59-component recipes.\n\nRelated insight: Recipe '14-5' demonstrates 39-component parametric workflows, further confirming the complexity range between simpler sequences and the most complex recipes.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe complexity upper bound: Recipe '14-6' demonstrates 73-component surface creation workflows, representing the highest complexity level observed in parametric surface creation recipes.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe S19E01 demonstrates 30-component surface creation workflows, providing a complexity data point between simpler 20-component recipes (S18E04) and mid-range 39-component workflows (14-5).\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe '3-1' adds a 71-component data point to the complexity progression: 30 components (S19E01) → 39 components (14-5) → 40 components (12-5) → 59 components (S11E04) → 71 components (3-1) → 73 components (14-6), showing refined granularity in high-complexity parametric surface workflows.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe complexity lower bound: Recipe '3-3-0' demonstrates 19-component parametric workflows, establishing a new lower complexity baseline in the progression: 19 components (3-3-0) → 30 components (S19E01) → 39 components (14-5) → 40 components (12-5) → 59 components (S11E04) → 71 components (3-1) → 73 components (14-6).\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe '3-3' provides a 62-component example in the 3-series, refining the complexity progression: 59 components (S11E04) → 62 components (3-3) → 71 components (3-1) → 73 components (14-6), showing more granular scaling in mid-to-high complexity parametric surface workflows.\n\nRelated insight: \n\nRelated insight: Recipe '06-01' demonstrates 47-component parametric workflows, filling the complexity gap between 40-component recipes (12-5) and 59-component workflows (S11E04), refining the mid-complexity range progression: 39 components (14-5) → 40 components (12-5) → 47 components (06-01) → 59 components (S11E04).\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe '06-02' demonstrates 42-component parametric workflows, refining the complexity progression between 40-component recipes (12-5) and 47-component workflows (06-01): 39 components (14-5) → 40 components (12-5) → 42 components (06-02) → 47 components (06-01) → 59 components (S11E04).\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe '10-1' demonstrates 68-component parametric workflows, refining the complexity progression between 62-component recipes (3-3) and 71-component workflows (3-1): 59 components (S11E04) → 62 components (3-3) → 68 components (10-1) → 71 components (3-1) → 73 components (14-6).\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe complexity new upper bound: Recipe '10-3' demonstrates 99-component surface creation workflows, establishing a new peak in the complexity progression: 19 components (3-3-0) → ... → 73 components (14-6) → 99 components (10-3), representing the most complex parametric surface workflow documented.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe '10-4' demonstrates 45-component parametric workflows, further refining the mid-complexity range between 42-component recipes (06-02) and 47-component workflows (06-01): 40 components (12-5) → 42 components (06-02) → 45 components (10-4) → 47 components (06-01) → 59 components (S11E04).\n\nRelated insight: Recipe 8-3 validates the 99-component ultra-complex tier alongside 10-3, confirming this as an established complexity category with multiple examples rather than a single outlier.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe '9-4' demonstrates 49-component parametric workflows, refining the complexity progression between 47-component recipes (06-01) and 59-component workflows (S11E04): 45 components (10-4) → 47 components (06-01) → 49 components (9-4) → 59 components (S11E04).\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe complexity new mega-complex tier: Unit-01-Class demonstrates 134-component surface creation workflows, establishing a new ultra-high complexity category that extends the progression: 19 components (3-3-0) → ... → 99 components (10-3, 8-3) → 134 components (Unit-01-Class), representing the most complex parametric surface workflow documented and creating a distinct mega-complex tier.",
